    <p>
        Launch your UDB and start a new map (<code>ctrl+n</code>). Game configuration dictates
        what features UDB will make available. For simplicity just pick a "Doom format"
        configuration matching the version of Doom you want to make a map for. So if you're
        mapping for Doom (1993) use <code>Doom: Doom (Doom format)</code>, and if you're
        mapping for Doom 2 (<span title="seriously, they could have cooked Doom 2 for way
        longer---probably should have">1994</span>) then you can use <code>Doom: Doom 2
        (Jazz&nbsp;Jackrabbit format)</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
        You'll also need to select the matching iWAD that contains all the textures and
        creatures that you'll be using (Doom or Jazz Jackrabbit or Doom 2, I guess).
    </p>

    <section class="image-strip">
        <a href="/static/img/doom-udb-draw-box-start.jpg">
            <img src="/static/img/doom-udb-draw-box-start.thumb.jpg" alt="UDB top-down grid view
